      <activity id="d5465bb7-4403-572a-a05c-9f188f8509da" activityNameId="432e849a-1b79-52e9-89c7-86340d26d454" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Particle board, melamin coated, doubleside coated (90 g</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Particle board, melamin coated, doubleside coated (90 g
na;
UUID: 17708259-c84d-33c3-9f10-adf22984af18
This data set includes the materials and resources needed for producing melamin coated plywood panels per m2. Both sides are melamin coated (90 g/m2). The panel is 16 mm wide. Melamin has a densitiy of 1574 kg/m3. This kind of melamin coated panels are used for corpus of cupboards and shelfs. Transport is estimated according to the ecoinvent standard distances for Switzerland. Linked to updated LCI of particle boards from Ecoinvent data v3.2 for KBOB recommendation 2016.; Geography: Data valid for Switzerland
Location: Data valid for Switzerland
Technology: Average processes for producing melamin coated plywood panels.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_17708259-c84d-33c3-9f10-adf22984af18.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
